==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
A Shetlandic and Orcadian alteration of ''[[trow]]'', most likely influenced by an unattested {{der|en|nrn|*drog||malevolent [undead] being}}. ''Trow'' is derived from {{der|en|nrn|troll}}, or otherwise from {{der|en|non|trǫll}}. L-vocalisation occurred in the early 15th century in Middle Scots, so "''[[troll|trolly]] [[knoll|knolls]]''" probably became "''trowie knowes''" around this time. The supposed Norn {{m|nrn|*drog}} would have been derived from {{cog|non|draugr}}.

